TITLE:: Arranger
SUMMARY:: Flow of sequence-name labels for the SequencerGui Arrange page.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/BorderView, Classes/SCViewHolder, Classes/Sequencer, Classes/SequencerGui

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::Arranger:: is a LINK::Classes/SCViewHolder:: that LINK::Classes/SequencerGui:: shows when the Arrange button is pressed. Its view uses a LINK::Classes/FlowLayout:: decorator. Each sequence name is a LINK::Classes/StaticText:: on a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: sized to that name, placed beside the previous label. Double-clicking a sequence calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-play:: with looping on and draws a border on that view. Double-clicking the sequence that is playing calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-stop:: and removes the border. Double-clicking a different sequence moves the border to that sequence.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates an instance of TELETYPE::Arranger::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: whose sequences this arranger lists and plays.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::Arranger:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addSequence
Adds a label for CODE::name::. A name that is already shown is left as it is.

ARGUMENT:: name
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::, displayed with CODE::asString::.

PRIVATE:: init, prSetBorder, prToggleSequence
